new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a844a85
--- /dev/null
+++ b/UTILIBRE-SOURCE.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+BiblioReads on Utilibre
+Upstream: https://github.com/nesaku/BiblioReads
+Revision: 9508abc64c6b35eef366e041fef47554f0ee888a
+License: AGPL-3.0-or-later; original license and notices retained.
+
+Local changes: bounded HTTPS-only server fetching with fixed upstream hosts and
+public-IP DNS pinning; request validation; same-origin cover-image proxy replacing
+wsrv.nl; current locked runtime dependencies; standalone Node 24 build; operator
+and privacy settings through the application's native configuration; matching
+source link in the existing source footer; one JSX lint fix.
+
+Build: docker build -f Dockerfile.utilibre -t utilibre-biblioreads:9508abc-p1 .
+Run using deployment/compose.biblioreads.yaml after adapting its host paths.
+The container is non-root, read-only, resource limited and has no request logs.
+The fixed-host guard requires utilibre-preload.cjs through Node --require.
+Gateway and host firewall settings are included in deployment/.
+
+Library records are browser-local. Use Library > Settings > Export to back up;
+clearing site data can erase them. The service worker may cache visited resources.
+Upstream Goodreads/Amazon and the separate Cloudflare/Caddy edge can see request
+metadata. This is not a confidential or end-to-end-encrypted reading service.
+
+The build retains upstream PWA tooling. npm audit --omit=dev reported zero
+advisories on 2026-10-06. The build-only dependency tree still has advisories;
+@ducanh2912/next-pwa and braces are absent from the standalone runtime image.
+Reassess both trees when updating; this is not a claim of vulnerability-free code.
